    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "The first paper analyzed 456 urban and peri-urban green patches in Lucknow, India, using satellite data from 2019 and 2024 to determine how patch size and vegetation condition influence surface-temperature contrasts. Another study developed TransMod, a unified forecasting framework designed to transfer spatio-temporal demand patterns from data-rich transportation modes to data-scarce ones. Finally, researchers evaluated state-of-the-art cross-city point-of-interest recommendation models using the large-scale Trip World benchmark.",
